invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_point.c
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: the doubling leaves out the step that doubles b, so b is X1 * r
  where the formula takes 2 * X1 * r, and h, X3 and Y3 come out for
  another point. No fault follows: every coordinate is still a field
  element. bin/p256_equiv_test holds the doubling to the complete
  addition of a point with itself on multiples of the generator and on
  the point at infinity.

--- old
    p256_wide_fe_mul(&b, &a->x, &r);
    p256_wide_fe_add(&b, &b, &b);
--- new
    p256_wide_fe_mul(&b, &a->x, &r);
